The Prosperity Passport’s launch has already demonstrated significant traction, with over 42,000 Prosperity Passports and 258,000 .celo domain names minted in its first 20 days. This rapid adoption highlights the demand for decentralized identity solutions in Web3. For Talent Protocol, this translates into a growing pool of verified users who can leverage their Prosperity Passports to enhance their Talent Passports, participate in DeFi opportunities, and connect with Celo’s mission-driven ecosystem.

Moreover, the Prosperity Passport aligns with Celo’s focus on regenerative finance (ReFi) and real-world asset (RWA) use cases, such as micro-loans and UBI, which are particularly relevant for Talent Protocol’s community of builders in emerging markets. Projects like Haraka and impactMarket, which facilitate micro-loans and UBI on Celo, demonstrate how Prosperity Passport holders can access financial tools that support their entrepreneurial goals, further amplifying Talent Protocol’s impact.

